    "kok_maddesi": "Back to library EtymArab SMQ سمق BP – • HDAL • © SG | 15Feb2021, last updated 19Mar2023 √SMQ “root” ▪ SMQ_1 ‘(to be) very high, towering, tall’ ↗ samaqa ▪ SMQ_2 ‘sumac (Rhus; bot. )’ ↗ summāq Other values, now obsolete, include (BK1860, Hava1899): ▪ † SMQ_3 ‘pure, mere | pur, franc, sans mélange’: † sumāq (esp. fig., kiḏb sumāq ‘mere lie’) ▪ † SMQ_4 ‘yoke | pièce de bois qui forme le joug des bœufs’: † samīqān i (du.) ▪ † SMQ_ ‘...’: † ... ▪ ... ▪ [v1] … ▪ [v2] : from Aram sūmaq , summāq , Syr sûmāqā ‘blood-red, dark red, reddish, ruddy; red lentil, red pottage; red\\purple dye, rouge, metaph. disguise; red ink, minium; ruby, sard; rhus coraria, sumach’, smaq ‘to be red, turn red’ (PayneSmith1903). – Lokotsch1927 #1946 also considers internal dependence on [v1], i.e., the sumac tree as the *‘high, beautifully-grown tree’. ▪ † [v3] … ▪ † [v4] … ▪ … – ▪ [v1] ... ▪ [v2] – (prob. loanword) ▪ † [v3] ... ▪ † [v4] ... ▪ ... ▪ ... ▪ [v2] Engl sumac , var. sumach , Fr sumac , etc. ↗ summāq ▪ ... – Sources ; meta ; gram ; engl ; conc ; hist ; cogn ; disc ; west ; deriv ;",
